      "reason": "The MCP JSON-RPC wire form is produced by each language's own JSON encoder, which is not part of the contract: Python's json.dumps inserts a space after every separator, and Go's encoding/json sorts map keys. The scripted assertions are structural (json_equals parses each line), so they are identical for all three targets and are what pins the protocol; only the raw bytes of the whole stream diverge. The error TEXT also diverges on Go: its reverse lookup replaces every underscore with a dot before giving up, so the name it reports back is not the name the caller sent. Asserted as $ANY here; pinned exactly by the two target-restricted cases below.",
